{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1110827-homebrew-dark-era-the-beast-part-of-my-congo-dark-era-is-done","id":1110827,"title":"[Homebrew Dark Era] The Beast part of my Congo Dark Era is done.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-03T06:58:42-07:00","id":1110827,"title":"[Homebrew Dark Era] The Beast part of my Congo Dark Era is done.","content":"Since November, I've been working on a Beast/Geist Dark Era set during King Leopold's domination of Congo; the Congo Free State Era. The pitch was essentially &quot;Heart Of Darkness&quot; Dark Era. You might have known this or not, but today I'm here to say that the Beast part is finally done.<br /> <br /> It's a <i>dark </i>Era indeed, but, as I've been saying since Beast's Kickstarter, I do think it resonates with many themes of Beast and Geist, and can be used to have an interesting game. I'm here to give you the link to it, since I think I did something decent with it. Something that is still rightfully subjected to criticism and far from being perfect, but stuff Beast fans might enjoy neverthless. More than anything, and I won't even lie about this, I'm posting it here because I'm looking forward to your feedback<br /> <br /> Alright, a couple of things.<br /> <br /> First of all, even in this form without the Geist part, the homebrew is rather big. Benefits (and issues) of not having to deal with word counts: I could do what I wanted to do while including everything I thought could be needed for the Dark Era. Those who know my previous homebrew (hello <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> ), know that I prefer to take my time and do things as best as I can. My Djinn homebrew was not short either, but it explored the idea completely and in a detailed way. A thing that came up as I was writing was the legitimate doubt about how some characters could happen, especially female ones. That's one of the reason I made tons of example characters: to show how Westerners and Africans, men and women, could be both Beast, Heroes and everything else. An attitude I plan to carry forward in the Geist part.<br /> <br /> Second, if you're familiar with my Beast ramblings across the forums, you're going to find some of my ideas shaping the writing and the characters. This was my first real big work about Beast and I inevitably tapped into my theories for it. Writer pours his ideas into his work and it shows, more news at 11. That's just to say you're going to find stuff that's familiar with what I usually say when I talk about Beast.<br /> <br /> Third, and I know this is a shameless self-promotion, this is not all. This is the Beast part. Geist will still happen and I'll also include general stuff, like pages about the other gamelines, corrections, crossover sections and ideas once everything else is done. You can already find traces of it in the document. Fancy way to say the ending result will be (hopefully) better. This is not the finished product, yadda yadda, more is to come, yadda yadda. But since this is a fan work and those live and prosper by feeding on attention, feedback and criticism, I'm already sharing the big part that's the completed Beast side of the Dark Era.<br /> <br /> Last, but not less important, i wish to say thanks to those good souls that have followed this project for all these months. Whether by writing comments and suggestions or by merely leaving a like, it's only thanks to them I managed to arrive this far and will find the determination to write the Geist parts. Thank you.<br /> <br /> This was a nice ride and I hope I'll enjoy even the rest of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 01-12-2021, 05:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T16:28:44-07:00","id":1111452,"title":"","content":"My god Cinder,this is amazing! Is as good as the Professional Dark eras! So cool!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T07:46:26-07:00","id":1111658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://foru